# Foursquare Places API — free tier, 1,000 calls/day, no credit card needed.
# IMPORTANT: The old "fsq3…" API keys are retired. You need a SERVICE KEY:
#   1. Go to https://developer.foursquare.com/ and sign in
#   2. Open your project → "Keys" tab → Generate a new Service Key
#   3. Paste that key below (it will look like a long Bearer token, not "fsq3…")
# Without a valid key the app falls back to Wikimedia + Wikipedia images.
VITE_FOURSQUARE_API_KEY="GWUOROAVISHKLN305SOHBPBBP3Y2WM22AWM5URN1VTYRXNBC"

# ── Venue Photos (Nearby tab) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add EITHER key below to get actual venue photos (like Google Maps shows).
#
# Option A — Google Places API (BEST quality, same source as Google Maps)
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com → Create project → Enable "Places API"
#   2. Create an API key (Maps Platform gives ~$200/month free credit = ~28k photos/mo)
#   3. Restrict the key to "Places API" + your domain for security
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY="AIzaSyBQgAp40gAXkZyVmr6_nXyhIGtJDhNPPI0"
#
# Option B — Yelp Fusion API (actual venue cover photos, 500 free req/day)
